nal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Vet</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Review: Measures to control house dust mites are not effective in patients with asthma who are sensitive to mites</article-title><source>ACP J Club</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>80</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b37"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Voorhorst</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Spieksma-Boezeman</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Spieksma</surname><given-names>FT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Is a mite (<italic>Dermatophagoides sp</italic>.) the producer of the house-dust allergen?</article-title><source>Allerg Asthma (Leipz)</source><year>1964</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14307280</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b38"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Der Veen</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jansen</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Aalberse</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Der p 1 and Der p 2 induce less severe late asthmatic responses than native <italic>Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus</italic> extract after a similar early asthmatic response</article-title><source>Clin Exp Allergy</source><year>2001</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>705</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11422129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b39"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Frederick</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bryant</surname><given-names>TN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Mech